{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793691590,"nonce":"TyyKOPXcylsRNhApLGLVA9/NKFE=","message":"Plan, 2026-11-03. Owner direction: the DSL leverages blinc_abi (layout, reactivity, scene, hit test, CSS) as ashui and blinc_ts do, with blinc_gpu as the renderer API. This is route C of the evaluation above; decision 3 is settled (R1, records are the pixel contract). Facts are measured unless marked read.\n\nWhat changed since the evaluation\n\n- blinc_gpu::display_list now draws what the evaluation listed as missing: boxes, glyph text over the producer's atlas, images and canvases, backdrops, layers (fade, blur, colour filter, drop shadow, masks), multi-stop and conic gradients, local, fading and clip-path clips, notches (read: fa2406c comments 4 to 14 and the display-list commits). Entry points: display_list::plan(floats, count, version, scale), then Painter::render(renderer, target, size, \u0026plan, clear, images); the producer's atlas goes in through GpuRenderer::set_glyph_atlas. Still open there: ce34b20 (data-texture packing) and mobile GPUs.\n- CSS coverage, measured with blinc_abi's blinc-css on Blinc's own sheets. CN_STYLES (1,976 lines) and UA_STYLES (301) are each one `@layer components` block, and the ABI engine skipped the whole block (\"@layer is not supported\"). Without the wrapper both parse with 0 diagnostics. Properties cn uses with no handler in the ABI: transform-origin (12 uses), SVG stroke (6), animation (52), transition (40), and 33 @keyframes (the ABI hands out keyframes by name; each SDK runs the motion). A clean parse is not proof a property is applied: declarations are kept as text and read when applied.\n- Done in the sibling repos today, uncommitted: blinc_abi @layer (statement, block, anonymous and nested forms; web ordering including reversed !important; one layer across sheets; compiled version 5 only for layered sheets) and transform-origin (PaintWrite::TransformOrigin, pivot in the display list and in hit testing). blinc_ts is wired (motion field, scene applier, docs, tests/native-css-layers.mjs). Tests: blinc_abi 200 with scene and 149 without, blinc_ts native 78; the new .mjs passes in both sheet formats and fails on the old addon. ashui-88 was told; ashui has no setter for the origin.\n- read: blinc_ts keeps its transition and animation engine in 4.9k lines of Rust (native/src/motion) on blinc_abi types. It is the piece blinc_abi lacks that the DSL, blinc_ts and ashui would otherwise each write.\n\nSteps, each landing alone\n\n0. blinc_abi gaps for cn's CSS: done (uncommitted), see above. Left: SVG fill and stroke as CSS, lengths in transform-origin, `@import ... layer()`.\n1. Dependency. Blinc consumes blinc_abi (default-features = false, features = [\"scene\"]) by path through a [patch.\"https://github.com/project-blinc/blinc\"] table, as the evaluation measured; one new crate (blinc_dsl_abi) depends on it and nothing else does.\n2. A DSL host interface (create, set, bind with Reactive tokens, insert, listen, dispose), the 120 builtins moved behind it, implemented over blinc_layout. Gate: the DSL suite unchanged (14 known failures).\n3. An ABI-backed host, headless: LayoutContext, GraphContext with host effects (1b04867), regions as insert_before and detach, disposal. Gate: the same programs give the same tree and the same records.\n4. blinc_gpu as the DSL's renderer API: a scene leaf element in blinc_app (R3) that owns a LayoutContext and a SceneEncoder, paints through plan and a Painter kept per window, and forwards pointer and key events to hit::test. API work in blinc_gpu: a frame entry taking records plus the atlas revision, and image and canvas slots owned by the leaf.\n5. Motion. Move the transition and animation engine into blinc_abi (or a crate all three share) so one implementation runs for the DSL, blinc_ts and ashui. Until then the ABI path cannot run cn's transitions and animations.\n6. The behaviour layer (decision 2), then cn as DSL components over CN_STYLES, with recorder goldens compared between the blinc_layout and ABI paths.\n\nOwner decisions\n- Route: C (host interface first) keeps cn and Rust widgets working through the move and gives a pixel comparison as the gate; A rewrites cn first. I recommend C.\n- \"blinc_css\": I read it as the CSS engine ashui and blinc_ts use, which is blinc_abi::css (they do not use Blinc's blinc_css crate). Blinc's blinc_css stays for blinc_layout. Confirm, because decision 5 (two engines) turns on it.\n- Behaviour layer (events, focus, text fields, scroll, overlays): reuse blinc_layout's router (bound to Div and RenderTree today), write it once in Rust for all SDKs (blinc_ts and ashui each re-implement it, about 23k lines of TypeScript for blinc_ts), or write it in the DSL.\n- Dependency direction (decision 4): the patch table (recommended; blinc_abi has its own [workspace] and a fat-LTO release profile) or blinc_abi as a workspace member.\n- Where motion lives (step 5).\n\nNot established: cn's pixels through the ABI path; event and focus routing through the ABI tree; SVG paint from CSS; performance.","files":null}]}